{"name":"Van Gogh Blue","hex":"#abddf1","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"van","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Valman."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A covered motor vehicle used to carry goods or (normally less than ten) persons, usually roughly cuboid in shape, Depending on the type of van, it can be bigger or smaller than a pickup truck and SUV, and longer and higher than a car but relatively smaller than a truck/lorry or a bus.","An enclosed railway vehicle for transport of goods, such as a boxcar/box van."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/van"},{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"}],"entries":[{"title":"Vincent van Gogh","blocks":[{"text":"Vincent Willem van Gogh was a Dutch Post-Impressionist painter who is among the most famous and influential figures in the history of Western art. In just over a decade he created about 2,100 artworks, including around 860 oil paintings, most of them in the last two years of his life. They include landscapes, still lifes, portraits and self-portraits, and are characterised by bold colours and dramatic, impulsive and expressive brushwork that contributed to the foundations of modern art. His suicide at age 37 followed years of mental illness and poverty."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Vincent_van_Gogh_-_Self-Portrait_-_Google_Art_Project_%28454045%29.jpg/330px-Vincent_van_Gogh_-_Self-Portrait_-_Google_Art_Project_%28454045%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vincent_van_Gogh"},{"title":"Van","blocks":[{"text":"A van is a type of road vehicle used for transporting goods or people. There is some variation in the scope of the word across the different English-speaking countries. The smallest vans, microvans, are used for transporting either goods or people in tiny quantities. Mini MPVs, compact MPVs, and MPVs are all small vans usually used for transporting people in small quantities. Larger vans with passenger seats are used for institutional purposes, such as transporting students. Larger vans with only front seats are often used for business purposes, to carry goods and equipment. Specially equipped vans are used by television stations as mobile studios. Postal services and courier companies use large step vans to deliver packages."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/2018_Ford_Transit_Custom_300_Base_2.0_facelift.jpg/330px-2018_Ford_Transit_Custom_300_Base_2.0_facelift.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Van"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Vincent_van_Gogh_January_1873_%28restored%29.jpg/500px-Vincent_van_Gogh_January_1873_%28restored%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Vincent_van_Gogh_January_1873_%28restored%29.jpg/500px-Vincent_van_Gogh_January_1873_%28restored%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AVincent_van_Gogh_January_1873_(restored).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/Theo_van_Gogh_May_1878_%28restored%29.jpg/500px-Theo_van_Gogh_May_1878_%28restored%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/Theo_van_Gogh_May_1878_%28restored%29.jpg/500px-Theo_van_Gogh_May_1878_%28restored%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATheo_van_Gogh_May_1878_(restored).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/e1/Koning_Willem_II_Hogere_Burgerschool_te_Tilburg_%281866%29_%28Vincent%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/e1/Koning_Willem_II_Hogere_Burgerschool_te_Tilburg_%281866%29_%28Vincent%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"Vincent van Gogh in 1866.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKoning_Willem_II_Hogere_Burgerschool_te_Tilburg_(1866)_(Vincent)_(cropped).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/48/Cuesmes_JPG001.jpg/500px-Cuesmes_JPG001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/48/Cuesmes_JPG001.jpg/500px-Cuesmes_JPG001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Van Gogh's home in Cuesmes; while there, he decided to become an artist","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACuesmes_JPG001.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Kee_Vos_met_zoon_Jan-cropped.jpg/500px-Kee_Vos_met_zoon_Jan-cropped.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Kee_Vos_met_zoon_Jan-cropped.jpg/500px-Kee_Vos_met_zoon_Jan-cropped.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Kee Vos-Stricker with her son Jan c. 1879–80","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKee_Vos_met_zoon_Jan-cropped.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Vincent_Willem_van_Gogh_016.jpg/500px-Vincent_Willem_van_Gogh_016.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Vincent_Willem_van_Gogh_016.jpg/1280px-Vincent_Willem_van_Gogh_016.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Vincent_Willem_van_Gogh_016.jpg/500px-Vincent_Willem_van_Gogh_016.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Rooftops, View from the Atelier The Hague, 1882, private collection","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AVincent_Willem_van_Gogh_016.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/Stilleven_met_bijbel_-_s0008V1962_-_Van_Gogh_Museum.jpg/250px-Stilleven_met_bijbel_-_s0008V1962_-_Van_Gogh_Museum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/Stilleven_met_bijbel_-_s0008V1962_-_Van_Gogh_Museum.jp